  "correction": "Use the existing canonical authority, egress and credential vault. One exact repository-key encrypted material write per existing durable approval. No plaintext in model, client DTO, errors, audit or provider body. A vault-authenticated producer proof prevents substituting arbitrary ciphertext even if an attacker recomputes a plain plan digest. Canonical digest remains stable through JSONB key reorder. No new orchestration, key, table, SQL, IAM, provider account or production resource.",
  "sourceProvenance": "Finite CSC/Apple name-to-provider mapping is server-owned. Canonical owner row must exist and remain unchanged around the existing authenticated vault consumer. No storage-mirror absence fallback authorizes a transfer. Preparation reads only the exact owner repository public key. Only opaque sealed-box bytes reach the confirmed PUT. A GitHub source-read credential check is not used as write authority.",
  "authority": "forceConfirmation is always true, CREDENTIAL_OR_PERMISSION_CHANGE, exact original owner/tenant, connected github repository, project, operation, destination, source/connection epoch and nonce. No boolean, raw user ID, serialized grant ID or fabricated context grants a write. Existing permission and claim SQL unchanged. Recheck current executing durable grant and expiry after consumption waits before PUT and result publication.",
  "recovery": "Producer proof is persisted in the same existing durable plan and uses the existing vault with owner/repository/nonce/parameter AAD. Synthetic provider reinitialization with the same test KEK passes. Existing managed KMS implementation and accepted Google migration evidence are unchanged, not rerun. A coordinated API/frontend release and security-compatible recovery image are required before activation. No deployment performed.",
  "functionality": "Preparation returns202 with display-only approvals and zero changed GitHub secrets. Actual UI requires a separate click for each exact material or uses canonical Cancel. Pipeline carries the original actor/signal and stops Actions dispatch while signing approval is pending. Unsigned operation when no material exists remains supported. No Actions, release-upload, store-publishing or upstream caller promotion is inferred.",
